> -----------
.         * 1.1 CONSTRUCT DEPENDENT VARIABLE: GenderEqualityHHᵢₜ
.         * -------------------------------------------------------------------
> -----------
.         * H3: Gender Equality in Household Behavior
.         * pid: p1_housework p1_childcare p1_caregiving p1_repairs
.         * pid_partner: 2_housework p2_childcare p2_caregiving p2_repairs
.         recode p*_housework p*_childcare p*_caregiving p*_repairs (-8 -5 -3 -
> 2 -1 = .)
(13,843 changes made to p1_housework)
(11,362 changes made to p2_housework)
(18,042 changes made to p1_childcare)
(16,318 changes made to p2_childcare)
(36,704 changes made to p1_caregiving)
(33,946 changes made to p2_caregiving)
(13,369 changes made to p1_repairs)
(11,874 changes made to p2_repairs)

.         
.         * Step 1: Calculate absolute differences in hours per domain (inequal
> ity)
.         gen diff_housework   = abs(p1_housework   - p2_housework)   if !missi
> ng(p1_housework, p2_housework)
(50,173 missing values generated)

.         gen diff_childcare   = abs(p1_childcare   - p2_childcare)   if !missi
> ng(p1_childcare, p2_childcare)
(56,244 missing values generated)

.         gen diff_caregiving  = abs(p1_caregiving  - p2_caregiving)  if !missi
> ng(p1_caregiving, p2_caregiving)
(74,624 missing values generated)

.         gen diff_repairs     = abs(p1_repairs     - p2_repairs)     if !missi
> ng(p1_repairs, p2_repairs)
(51,476 missing values generated)

. 
.         * Step 2: Calculate average inequality across all valid domains (0 = 
> equality)
.         egen GenderInequality = rowmean(diff_housework diff_childcare diff_ca
> regiving diff_repairs)
(41,442 missing values generated)

. 
.         * Step 3: Reverse code to obtain equality measure (higher = more equa
> lity)
.         * Note: This rescales the variable based on the maximum observed ineq
> uality
.         summarize GenderInequality if GenderInequality < ., meanonly

.         gen GenderEqualityHH = r(max) - GenderInequality
(41,442 missing values generated)

.         label variable GenderEqualityHH "Behavioral Gender Equality (rescaled
> )"

. 
