.         /* We assume that GenderEqualityHH, a continuous measure of behaviora
> l gender equality in the household (based on the relative division of labor b
> etween partners), reflects support for gender equality (Hypothesis 3).
>            Accordingly, we run a random-effects linear panel regression with 
> GenderEqualityHH as the dependent variable and DaughterHH (categorical: child
>  gender composition) as the key independent variable.
>            Control variables include gender (Woman), number of children, sexu
> al orientation, parental religion (mother/father), age, and region.
>            Due to collinearity, partnership status was omitted from the model
> .
>            We use panel-robust standard errors and cluster at the individual 
> level (pid).
>         */
. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.                 * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[3.DaughterHH]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[3.DaughterHH]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "z" // Adapted by DA during consiten
> cy check

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value // Adapted by DA during consitency check
.                 local z_stat = _b[3.DaughterHH] / _se[3.DaughterHH]

.                 local p_value = 2 * (1 - normal(abs(`z_stat')))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

